neutron-zzzzzzzzzzzs-DIAG-d2d1-nb-vs-union-probe

DIAGNOSTIC ONLY (patches/diagnostic). Prints, never gates. Ships in no release.

THE QUESTION. The DC-direct present already reports `blitCoverage` = union_px / client_px per
window every 200 presents. In the 2026-08-21 timeline capture the 3640x604 timeline container
sat at 40-97% per 200-present window, which killed the "copy only the dirty region" lever for
the pre-draw hook (PERFORMANCE.md 2026-09-13). But that union is nb UNION nc, and nc is a
clip SUPERSET: glyph runs, geometries and Clear fold the current clip -- or the WHOLE target
when nothing is pushed -- into it (neutron_dr_add_clip). If the high coverage is nc inflating
the union, the real dirty area is smaller and tightening the union would pay on BOTH copies
(pre-draw hook + present readback, together ~20% of wall time). One session answers it.

WHAT IT ADDS, on the same DC-DIRECT line:
    nbCoverage=N%   nb_px / client_px -- the EXACT-rect half alone, same +2 fringe, same clamp,
                    same denominator as blitCoverage
    unionFrames=N   presents that accumulated into union_px
    nbFrames=N      of those, presents where nb contributed
    ncFrames=N      presents where nc contributed at all
    ncFull=N        presents where nc ALONE covered >= 95% of the client -- the signature of an
                    unclipped glyph/geometry/Clear inflating the union

READING IT: nbCoverage ~= blitCoverage => the 40-97% is genuinely dirty and the enquiry is
closed. nbCoverage much smaller (and ncFull high) => we over-report our own dirty rects.

⛔ A PROBE MUST NOT CHANGE THE PATH IT OBSERVES (OPTRACE disabled the fast path it measured;
LAYER_TRACE inverted a lock from inside the flush callback). This one: reads context fields
that neutron_dr_get_union() already reads from the same caller on the same thread; takes no
lock; performs no D3D or win32u call; adds no branch that touches uv, u, the blit or drawing;
its only output is five extra fields on a log line that already prints at that cadence.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/d2d1_private.h
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/d2d1_private.h
@@ -93,6 +93,8 @@
  * union (device pixels) as a RECT, for clipping the DC-direct blit-back. Defined in
  * device.c. */
 void neutron_dr_get_union(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt, RECT *out, BOOL *valid);
+/* NEUTRON DIAG nb-vs-union: the two halves of that union separately (device.c). */
+void neutron_dr_get_union_parts(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt, RECT *nb, BOOL *nb_valid, RECT *nc, BOOL *nc_valid);
 
 /* NEUTRON op-trace: per-frame op/clear stats for the DC-direct present diagnostic. */
 void neutron_dr_get_frame_stats(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt, unsigned *ops, unsigned *clears, RECT *clear_rect);
@@ -896,6 +898,15 @@
      * what makes a stale bitmap stomp the window's GDI-drawn content. */
     unsigned long long union_px;
     unsigned long long client_px;
+    /* NEUTRON DIAG nb-vs-union (2026-09-13, patches/diagnostic): is the union above inflated by
+     * the nc clip-superset fallback (glyph runs / geometries / Clear with no clip pushed fold
+     * the WHOLE target into nc)? nb_px counts the EXACT-rect half of the same union alone,
+     * with the same +2 fringe and clamp as u; nc_frames = frames where nc contributed at all;
+     * nc_full_frames = frames where nc alone covered >= 95% of the client. union_frames =
+     * frames that accumulated into union_px. Accumulate-only: nothing reads these except the
+     * DC-DIRECT report line. */
+    unsigned long long nb_px;
+    unsigned int union_frames, nb_frames, nc_frames, nc_full_frames;
     /* NEUTRON PERF: cumulative stage timings (QPC ticks) + worst case, per container. */
     LONGLONG perf_wdc, perf_readback, perf_blit, perf_total;
     /* NEUTRON PERF: the OTHER half of a frame -- how long the app's own drawing takes
--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -1492,6 +1492,23 @@
     else *valid = FALSE;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON DIAG nb-vs-union (2026-09-13): the two halves of the union above, separately, so the
+ * DC-DIRECT report can say how much of union_px the exact-rect half (nb) accounts for. Reads the
+ * same fields neutron_dr_get_union() reads, from the same caller, on the same thread, under no
+ * additional lock. It does not write context state and changes nothing about what is drawn or
+ * blitted -- a probe must not alter what it observes (see the OPTRACE and LAYER_TRACE incidents). */
+void neutron_dr_get_union_parts(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt, RECT *nb, BOOL *nb_valid, RECT *nc, BOOL *nc_valid)
+{
+    struct d2d_device_context *context = impl_from_ID2D1DeviceContext((ID2D1DeviceContext6 *)rt);
+
+    if ((*nb_valid = !!context->nb_valid))
+        SetRect(nb, (LONG)context->nb_l, (LONG)context->nb_t,
+                (LONG)(context->nb_r + 0.999f), (LONG)(context->nb_b + 0.999f));
+    if ((*nc_valid = !!context->nc_valid))
+        SetRect(nc, (LONG)context->nc_l, (LONG)context->nc_t,
+                (LONG)(context->nc_r + 0.999f), (LONG)(context->nc_b + 0.999f));
+}
+
 static HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE d2d_device_context_inner_QueryInterface(IUnknown *iface, REFIID iid, void **out)
 {
     NEUTRON_API_TIME();
